# Duplicate team page - 2026-07-28. /team/corey-peterson/ was an orphan copy of
# /team/djs/corey/ with zero inbound links, sitting in sitemap.xml and burning
# crawl budget while never being crawled. Forced (!) because the old file still
# exists on disk and Netlify serves real files before non-forced rules.
/team/corey-peterson/ /team/djs/corey/ 301!

# Retired lead tracker - 2026-08-06. /tracker-legacy/ was the pre-cutover tracker
# (see db6df9f, 2026-06-17). Its only protection was a guessable sync code typed
# into an anonymous Firebase session, so anyone who knew a code could read another
# DJ's leads - which is the whole reason /tracker/ moved to email + password.
# The page is deleted; this sends old bookmarks to the new login screen.
# NOTE: the Firestore 'trackers/{syncCode}' data is deliberately NOT deleted -
# the new tracker's one-time import still reads it (tracker/index.html:1477).
/tracker-legacy/* /tracker/ 301!

